This one-weight example uses a loss of weight times weight, whose gradient is 2 times weight. It shows the two actions without a whole network.

```javascript
let weight = 2;
const gradient = 2 * weight;
console.log(weight);
weight = weight - 0.1 * gradient;
console.log(weight);
```

The first line printed is 2. Only after the update does it print 1.6.
